WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.247
This query demonstrates one of the safest patterns
for analytical joins Each

00:00:06.274 --> 00:00:10.458
common table expression summarizes one child table
to one row per patient

00:00:11.382 --> 00:00:16.684
Admission counts has one patient row Lab counts has
one patient row

00:00:17.605 --> 00:00:23.228
Prescription counts has one patient row Only after
those summaries

00:00:23.254 --> 00:00:28.188
are created do we join them to patients Run the
query and

00:00:28.215 --> 00:00:34.507
inspect the patient IDs Each patient should appear
exactly once Patients

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.994
with no matching activity are preserved because the
joins are LEFT JOINs

00:00:38.257 --> 00:00:43.878
and COALESCE converts missing counts to zero This
structure makes the grain

00:00:43.904 --> 00:00:48.539
easy to defend The final result is one row per
patient because

00:00:48.565 --> 00:00:53.682
every source being joined is already at patient
grain The query is

00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:57.261
a little longer than directly joining all detail
tables but it is

00:00:57.274 --> 00:01:02.790
much easier to validate In analytical SQL clarity
and correctness are usually

00:01:02.803 --> 00:01:05.013
more valuable than saving a few lines
